<%# The share control (story 0031). Locals: painting (required).
    Rendered only when `painting.display_image?` — a resting work has no file
    to hand off. Sits immediately LEFT of the keep control everywhere it
    appears: keep and its count share a Turbo frame that grows when the
    private fragment lands (`favorites/_control.html.erb`), and DESIGN.md's
    own rule is that nothing may sit to that frame's right for exactly this
    reason. Left of it, the frame's growth never touches this button.

    Public and unconditional in the markup: unlike the keep frame, this is
    the SAME button for every visitor, shell or browser, cookieless or not —
    it carries no form, no CSRF token, no session, nothing a public cache
    could leak. `/`'s `Cache-Control: public` contract survives this
    unconditionally, which is why there is no server-side branch here at all.

    Hidden by default (`.rail__share`'s CSS), revealed only inside a shell
    whose Hotwire Native bridge registered the `"share"` component. That
    reveal is a plain `<html data-shell-share>` attribute stamped by an
    inline script in `layouts/_head.html.erb` before this element ever
    paints — see that file for why the mechanism is a User-Agent read rather
    than the bridge's own (later-arriving) dataset.

    `data-controller="bridge--share"` extends the Hotwire Native Bridge
    package's own `BridgeComponent` base class, which independently refuses
    to CONNECT at all outside a matching shell (`static get shouldLoad`) —
    belt and braces: a reader who somehow sees this button in a plain browser
    taps a control with no controller attached, a safe no-op.

    Momentary, not a toggle: no `aria-pressed`, no fill state. Fill is the
    house's OWN-STATE marker (keep, the wing door) and share does not have
    one — tapping it does not change anything about the painting. %>
<% payload = share_payload_for(painting) %>
<button type="button" class="rail__act rail__share"
        data-controller="bridge--share"
        data-action="bridge--share#share"
        data-bridge--share-text-value="<%= payload[:text] %>"
        data-bridge--share-url-value="<%= payload[:url] %>"
        data-bridge--share-image-path-value="<%= payload[:image_path] %>"
        aria-label="Share <%= painting.title %>">
  <%# The platform's own square-and-arrow, redrawn in the house hand — 1.4px
      stroke, 23px drawing, `--gold` via `currentColor`. Not an invented
      brand mark: the rail is label-less and only `/`'s "N kept" teaches a
      glyph's meaning, so share's meaning has to arrive already known, and
      this is the one mark every iOS reader already carries (design review
      D4, 2026-08-31). %>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="23" height="23" aria-hidden="true"
       fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"
       stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
    <path d="M12 15.5V4.5M12 4.5 7.8 8.9M12 4.5l4.2 4.4"/>
    <path d="M5.5 12.5v6.2c0 .77.63 1.4 1.4 1.4h10.2c.77 0 1.4-.63 1.4-1.4v-6.2"/>
  </svg>
</button>
